From: Abinash Haldorai <abinash.haldorai@eka.care>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:11:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Integrations: let an agent binding say where phone calls
 can be handed to a person

Add an optional "handover" block to the agent product config on a
binding:

  {"handover": {"number": "+919999911111",
                "hours": {"start": "09:00", "end": "18:00", "timezone": "Asia/Kolkata"},
                "ring_seconds": 30}}

number is the staff phone (E.164, normalised, not the clinic's public
number). hours is optional (absent means always available; start after end
means overnight). ring_seconds is 10 to 60. Unknown keys are rejected, as
for every config here.

It lives on the binding config rather than the number's credentials
because matrix reads it from the shared Postgres and cannot decrypt
credentials. Other channels ignore it.

The phone-number rules move out of the Vobiz schema into
integration/schemas/phone.py so both use the same one.

The binding form lists a product's config fields as callback boxes; limit
that to fields that hold a Callback, so handover is neither shown as a
callback nor wiped when the form is saved.

No console form yet; the binding API accepts it today. Not tested against
a database.

